  "why": "Raw GraphQL evidence for two questions only: which head a thread was raised on, and whether it is still unresolved. Closure by written disposition is a MANUAL, human-verified step and is deliberately not modelled here. Four attempts to encode it -- a computed origin OID, a boolean, an invented id mapping, and a preselected artifact list -- each moved the authority decision somewhere the test could not see, ending with a matcher that would let a comment on another PR saying \"Still unresolved: <url>\" close a thread. Parsing free-form prose to automate a manual gate manufactures authority that does not exist.",
